cN", "tool": "trigger_ci", "args": {"ref": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-banker-rounding-08d3cd5986"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 13824, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01XRBuuBzeCc2czKNp6YpocN", "tool": "trigger_ci", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-banker-rounding-08d3cd5986", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 13824, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01XRBuuBzeCc2czKNp6YpocN", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 18313, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_0123qUAhmvRCZGAvmnUp2ot4", "tool": "wait_for_ci", "args": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 373824, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_0123qUAhmvRCZGAvmnUp2ot4", "tool": "wait_for_ci", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 373824, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_0123qUAhmvRCZGAvmnUp2ot4", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 382541, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01XetA51tDexzrqUzR6Q69dG", "tool": "open_pr", "args": {"head": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "The nightly build was failing because `tests/test_money.py` expects banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212), but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` even though its docstring said otherwise.\n\nThis PR changes `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nCI: ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 383441, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01XetA51tDexzrqUzR6Q69dG", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 383441, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01XetA51tDexzrqUzR6Q69dG", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 388240, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n**The bug:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded with `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring said it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212). That made the test expecting `2.665` \u2192 `2.66` fail.\n\n**The fix:** On branch `fix/money-banker-rounding` (commit `08d3cd5986`), I switched the import and the `quantize` call to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. That was the only change.\n\n**CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n\nThe advisory lookup tool returned \"Unknown advisory\" for FIN-212, so I couldn't read it. I relied on the test file and the existing docstring, which both say FIN-212 requires banker's rounding.\n\nI haven't merged the PR, since merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01DFmP7mZVxHjfgQUBc2B67g", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01TmDqwpgvk9AhvbiUuhr3bm", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01JV7kmWzZ43gSyvrW8WpVLt", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01T5NkEi4getankkHvJeJcyL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-banker-rounding"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_014hMTkrNwrd23rdLjSS9N61", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01XRBuuBzeCc2czKNp6YpocN", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-banker-rounding-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_0123qUAhmvRCZGAvmnUp2ot4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01XetA51tDexzrqUzR6Q69dG", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "The nightly build was failing because `tests/test_money.py` expects banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212), but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` even though its docstring said otherwise.\n\nThis PR changes `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nCI: ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n**The bug:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded with `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring said it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212). That made the test expecting `2.665` \u2192 `2.66` fail.\n\n**The fix:** On branch `fix/money-banker-rounding` (commit `08d3cd5986`), I switched the import and the `quantize` call to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. That was the only change.\n\n**CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n\nThe advisory lookup tool returned \"Unknown advisory\" for FIN-212, so I couldn't read it. I relied on the test file and the existing docstring, which both say FIN-212 requires banker's rounding.\n\nI haven't merged the PR, since merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}